timing: |
  Two register stages. A and B are sampled at rising edge k (stage 1: products),
  dot_out is updated at rising edge k+1 (stage 2: sum). A new A/B pair is accepted every cycle.
  During reset dot_out is 0.
  Race-free testbench: drive A and B on a falling edge, and check dot_out two falling edges
  later (after two rising edges), before driving anything else that would change it.
  Expected values: dot_out = sum over i of A[i]*B[i], with A[i] = A[i*WIDTH +: WIDTH] as a
  signed WIDTH-bit number (same for B). Example above: 96.


